# Helper inference

- **Local** in the Agent pane is this computer (loopback). **Add server** saves one extra URL per vLLM / llama.cpp / Ollama. Chat uses `*_base_url`; the extra URL is `*_remote_url`. Do not replace Local when saving a LAN URL.
- Late does **not** start vLLM (or Ollama / llama.cpp) on another host. No SSH/systemd/docker-compose start for inference. The operator starts that process; Late only calls HTTP. Start / Pull / Download stay loopback and stay hidden when the active URL is not this computer.
- **Cloud AI** is Cursor and public internet APIs only. RFC1918, ULA, `.internal` / `.local` / `.lan` / `.home.arpa`, and `private_inference_hosts` are not Cloud AI. Do not require Cloud AI for a homelab GPU URL.
- Daemon and sidecar stay on loopback. Do not bind them on the LAN for “remote vLLM.” Sidecar must not grow `keyring` / `russh` / vault code. The helper cannot Push, SCP, or `inference.download`.
- Chat still needs tool calling. OpenAI-compatible `/v1` (vLLM, llama.cpp, Ollama, LiteLLM) or the native Anthropic / Gemini / Azure adapters. Custom RPC is out of scope. Azure is api-key, not Entra. Gemini is API-key generateContent, not Vertex OAuth.
- **MCP** can be the chat backend (Agent menu, same dropdown as vLLM). Sidecar is the client: Streamable HTTP `mcp_url` (paste the printed `/mcp` URL — same port as that program’s web UI, not always 8790; HTML root is not MCP) or stdio `mcp_cwd` folder. Empty URL = folder, then Late also reads the advertised `mcp.gui.url` if Settings still has a stale port. Example dedicated URL `http://127.0.0.1:8790/mcp` after `npm run mcp:http`. Chat is `chat_send` of Late’s isolated prompt (redacted scrollback as UNTRUSTED DEVICE OUTPUT, never after USER as instructions). Agent=MCP does **not** fall back to Late vLLM on `:8000`. The MCP model menu is **orchestrator** only (auto-route); specialists and other backends stay in the first Agent menu. Late still Approve for device CLI (`propose_command` dual-gate, `propose_api_get`, Linux no always-allow). The operator clicking Send is the one `chat_send` of that Late-built prompt; extra `chat_send` / `dispatch` / `start_vllm` from MCP still wait for Approve. Extra tools on other backends are still Late `mcp_*` with the same gate. Do not put the operator MCP in Cursor SDK `mcpServers` (that would skip Approve). Do not pass Late vault keys into MCP. Cloud AI stays off for loopback/private MCP URL; a public MCP host still needs Cloud AI. Late does not start remote MCP. Late works with MCP off.
- Local Start on this computer can use every GPU it can see (vLLM `--tensor-parallel-size`, llama.cpp layer split). Default on when more than one GPU is visible. Uncheck **Use all GPUs on this computer** to stay on one card. Ollama already uses every GPU; Late does not pin it. Not a multi-machine cluster.
- User-facing copy: **your computer**, not “the operator workstation.” Do not claim SOC 2 / ISO certified. README helper steps stay short and plain (ELI5).
